<h1 class="page-title">ER:LC Integration</h1>
<p class="page-desc">Connect BotNexus to your Emergency Response: Liberty County server for live logs and session tools.</p>

<h2 id="connecting-your-erlc-server">Connecting your ER:LC server</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li class="step">
    <h4>Open the ER:LC module</h4>
    <p>Run <code class="inline">/erlcsetkey</code>.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="step">
    <h4>Add your server key</h4>
    <p>Paste your in-game server key when prompted. BotNexus only uses it to read server and player status.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="step">
    <h4>Pick a log channel</h4>
    <p>Choose where logs should post.</p>
  </li>
</ol>

<h2 id="what-gets-synced">What gets synced</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Player count</strong> — synced automatically. If you've set up an ER:LC status VC with
  <code class="inline">/statuschannel</code>, it updates in real time.</li>
  <li><strong>Sessions</strong> — scheduled sessions post automatically and can pull live player counts.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
<p>If logs stop appearing, re-check the server key first — ER:LC rotates keys periodically. Re-run the
<strong>ER:LC Integration</strong> module and paste the current key to reconnect.</p>

